in the vast back catalog of superhero  movies slowly making their way to the  screen after the great hollywood  bottleneck of 2020  few entries are as highly anticipated as  the suicide squad  the behind the scenes story behind the  franchise do-over is dramatic enough to  warrant its own blockbuster  after a tactical trolling at the hands  of social media users  guardians of the galaxy director james  gunn was briefly let go by disney  only to have warner brothers snatch him  up a few months later as a result  the dc universe is getting its own gun  brand crew of misfits  using david ayer's critically disastrous  hyper-lucrative 2016 original as a  jumping-off point the film is set to  introduce  a wide array of new anti-heroes to the  dc eu  while expanding on the ones we've  already met but despite a near universal  faith and gun's ability to turn the  suicide squad into a success story  fans have been vocally wondering about  the absence of a certain big league star  first introduced in the 2016 movie but  nowhere to be found here  so just why aren't we getting more of  jared leto's joker in  the suicide squad dc fans will remember  that jared leto's joker was a shot heard  around the nerd world when he first  appeared in promotional images for david  ayers suicide squad  a whole mountain of expectations were  piled on his milky white shoulders  in the lead up to that movie this was  supposed to be a fresh  new joker more unhinged than ever before  and at long last paired with his squeeze  harley quinn on the big screen leto  himself only added fuel to the fire  describing the part in interviews as a  chance to  strike new ground with a beloved villain  sadly the results were mixed at best  die-hard fans of this decidedly edgier  take on the joker are few  and far between as a truncated edit and  less than grounded story left letto's  joker largely underdeveloped and  underutilized  leto would only graze the screen for  about 10 minutes of the two-hour movie  and didn't do much even when he was  around in the eyes of many it just  didn't feel like he had much to do in a  story about extorted pyrokinetics  and extra dimensional sorceresses james  gunn as it turns out  agreed with that assessment and said as  much in a recent interview with the new  york times  asked about whether he considered  bringing leto's joker back into the fray  the filmmaker didn't mince words saying  joker no i just don't know why joker  would be in the suicide squad he  wouldn't be helpful in that type of war  situation  gunn has a point too despite the strange  implications of the justice league  snyder cut sepia tone to epilogue it's  hard to imagine trying to keep a madcap  homicidal clown on the straight and  narrow during a fight harley quinn seems  like enough of a handful on her own and  her sense of morality at least  places her firmly in the anti-hero camp  but the joker enjoys a steadfastly  chaotic evil approach to life  in short he's not a team player  additionally with a pool of more than a  dozen new characters already in play  adding leto's joker to the suicide squad  probably felt like something of a trap  overreaching to include one of the  world's most recognizable villains in  the series first installment was likely  a once bitten  scenario for the studio not only that  but margot robbie has distanced herself  from the portrayal of joker and harley's  relationship in the years since suicide  squad  take that into account and shoehorning  leto into the new story becomes an  even more complicated affair on the  upside mr j's absence doesn't mean that  there won't be plenty of big budget  blockbuster slaughter to go around  gun has been nothing if not clear about  his willingness to gleefully kill off as  many of his characters as he wants at  the drop of a hat  the body counts will be firmed up when  the suicide squad hits theaters and hbo  max on august 5th  2021 check out one of our newest videos  right here plus even more looper videos  about your favorite movies are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss  a single one  you
 

